**/node_modules
**/dist
.git
# Every env file, at any depth.
#
# `.env` alone matches only the repository root. `frontend/.env` was NOT excluded, and
# the frontend build stage does `COPY frontend/ ./` -- so a developer's local env file
# was copied into the image, where Vite would read it and inline its values into the
# bundle, silently overriding the VITE_API_BASE_URL that compose passed as a build arg.
#
# The direct consequence is a build that depends on whoever ran it. The worse one is
# that nothing stopped somebody putting a non-VITE secret in that file and baking it
# into an image layer, where it stays after the file is deleted.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
docs
*.md
